ID: B2-Ch11a-Intro
TEXT:

set(v_b2_ch11_added_hearing,1) if (v_b2_ch10_activate == 1 && v_b2_ch11_added_hearing == 0 && v_b2_ch6_stat == 1 && v_b2_ch9_channel == 1 && v_ch11_saved_rose == 0)
set(v_hearing,+3) if (v_b2_ch10_activate == 1 && v_b2_ch11_added_hearing == 0 && v_b2_ch6_stat == 1 && v_b2_ch9_channel == 1 && v_ch11_saved_rose == 0)
set(v_hearing_aux,+3) if (v_b2_ch10_activate == 1 && v_b2_ch11_added_hearing == 0 && v_b2_ch6_stat == 1 && v_b2_ch9_channel == 1 && v_ch11_saved_rose == 0)
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
 

"You're right..." Daren tells Hadrik, scanning the motionless canopy. "Time is frozen solid. Is this Eiden's doing?"

"Not Eiden," Arraka says from the amulet. "If Eiden were anywhere near here, I would have told you, remember?"

"Then who?" Daren asks. "Who else freezes time across an entire forest?"

"Why don't you look toward the trees and find out?" Arraka says. "She is walking right toward you."

"She?..." Daren says.

Between the frozen pines, a solitary figure emerges. Rose walks toward us with slow, measured steps, her eyes burning with pure yellow light. Her face is blank stone, staring straight through the clearing without acknowledging any of us.

"The revenant," Daren says, his voice going cold. "Come on. Let's see what it wants."

We close the distance. Ten paces out, the revenant halts in mid-stride. Her yellow stare stays locked on the horizon, features completely inert.

"Why are you here, revenant?" Daren demands. "Why did you freeze time?"

No flinch, no blink. The creature stands in absolute silence, locked deep in a trance.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1) {
 

"You're right..." Daren tells Hadrik, scanning the motionless canopy. "Time is frozen solid. Is this Eiden's doing?"

"Not Eiden," Arraka says from the amulet. "If Eiden were anywhere near here, I would have told you, remember?"

"Then who?" Daren asks. "Who else freezes time across an entire forest?"

"Why don't you look toward the trees and find out?" Arraka says. "She is walking right toward you."

"She?..." Daren says.

Between the frozen pines, a solitary figure emerges. Rose walks toward us with slow, measured steps, her eyes burning with pure yellow light. Her face is blank stone, staring straight through the clearing without acknowledging any of us.

"Rose?..." Daren says. "Wasn't she in Thilias yesterday? Come on—let's get closer!"

We hurry over. The moment we reach her, Rose halts in mid-stride, staring straight ahead with the same vacant, glowing gaze.

"Rose, can you hear us?" Kate calls out.

Not a breath changes. Rose stands stiff as wood, lost to the world in a deep trance.

}
choice("Keep trying to talk to her.", B2-Ch11a-Keep, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11a-Keep, v_checkpoint_rich = 0)
choice("Grab her by the arms, and try to shake her out of the trance.", B2-Ch11a-Grab, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11a-Grab, v_checkpoint_rich = 0)


ID: B2-Ch11a-Keep
TEXT:

#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
 "Are you listening to us?..." I say.

The revenant stays rigid. I step directly into her field of view and snap my fingers inches from her nose.

"Come on," I say. "Snap out of it."

"Oh, no..." Melindra says. "I've seen this before. If this is what I think it is, get ready. That sage fight is going to look like a stroll in the park compared to what's coming."

"They're in for a treat, alright!" Arraka cackles from the gold casing.

"What are you two on about?" Hadrik asks. "Ready for what?"

"It's starting," Melindra says.

The revenant vanishes from the spot. Her voice rings out from behind us, thick with heavy reverberation, and we spin around to find her already standing twenty paces back. The voice carries none of Rose's warmth—only a hollow, resonant drone.

"A prophecy, I have come to tell you..." the revenant intones.

"Here we go," Arraka says.

"A prophecy of things that may come to pass, but which have not yet been set in stone," the revenant continues. "Listen carefully to the events foretold, and you may prevent them before it is too late."

She blinks out of existence again, reappearing on our left flank. The echo in her voice deepens, rattling our teeth. With every line she speaks, she shifts to a new position in the blink of an eye, keeping our heads snapping back and forth.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1) {
 "Rose!" I shout. "Hey, Rose!"

She gives no sign of hearing. I move directly in front of her and wave my hand across her face.

"Nothing," I say. "Her pupils don't even track."

"Oh, no..." Melindra says. "I've seen this before. If this is what I think it is, get ready. That sage fight is going to look like a stroll in the park compared to what's coming."

"They're in for a treat, alright!" Arraka cackles from the gold casing.

"What are you two on about?" Hadrik asks. "Ready for what?"

"It's starting," Melindra says.

Rose vanishes from the spot. Her voice rings out from behind us, thick with heavy reverberation, and we spin around to find her already standing twenty paces back. The voice carries none of Rose's warmth—only a hollow, resonant drone.

"A prophecy, I have come to tell you..." Rose intones.

"Here we go," Arraka says.

"A prophecy of things that may come to pass, but which have not yet been set in stone," Rose continues. "Listen carefully to the events foretold, and you may prevent them before it is too late."

She blinks out of existence again, reappearing on our left flank. The echo in her voice deepens, rattling our teeth. With every line she speaks, she shifts to a new position in the blink of an eye, keeping our heads snapping back and forth.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch11a-Prophecy, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11a-Prophecy)


ID: B2-Ch11a-Grab
TEXT:

#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
 I step forward and take the revenant by the arms. The instant my fingers make contact, a violent burst of magical force repels me, throwing me flat onto my back in the dirt.

"What the hell?..." I grumble, pushing myself upright.

"Oh, no..." Melindra says. "I've seen this before. If this is what I think it is, get ready. That sage fight is going to look like a stroll in the park compared to what's coming."

"They're in for a treat, alright!" Arraka cackles from the gold casing.

