TEXT:

 "You really are starting to get on my nerves, you know that?"

"Because I laugh at your friend?" Arraka asks. "Thicken your skin, Barry. The world doesn't hand out soft cushions."

"Maybe I'll try ignoring you," I say.

"And forfeit my commentary? You're not that foolish."

In the street, Eiden reads Daren's aura reset for the second time.

"I must refrain from interfering," Eiden repeats with a smile.

"No!" Daren pleads, desperation cracking his voice. "I need your power! The power to strike the noble!"

