"No," Arraka corrects. "That rule applies only to our projection. The realms your companions occupy are entirely physical parallel timelines branch-locked from the moment of divergence. Changes there won't rewrite our timeline, but the danger to their minds is absolute. Did you think your trial was forgiving? That was Selkram manipulating the outcome to wring out despair."

"Selkram..." The name tastes like bile. "Is he watching us right now?"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch11a-Materialized, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11a-Materialized)


ID: B2-Ch11a-Materialized
TEXT:

 "No," Arraka says. "Maintaining a physical avatar on the earthen plane drains too much energy. He manifests only at the opening and conclusion of a trial, unless a catastrophic failure forces his hand. Otherwise, he remains in the magical plane, gathering the harvest."

"What does he gain from these trials?" I ask.

"Raw negative emotion," Arraka explains. "Hatred, panic, grief, despair. Highly concentrated psychic resonance. Without a host of mortal worshipers, he relies on the Magium link during a weaver's trance to siphon power from pivotal souls. The trials are engineered specifically to break you."

"And Kate's trial takes place in the Beacon?"

"We are about to find out," Arraka says. "I haven't scanned this sequence yet—we'll experience it together. Let's look in."

The screaming corridor dissolves.

We materialize in a cramped, windowless stone cell lit by a single narrow vent near the ceiling. An eleven-year-old Kate, dressed in coarse gray rags, leans close to a frail blonde girl of twelve—Diane. Kate's features are instantly recognizable, smaller and sharper, while Diane looks delicate and malnourished compared to the woman I met in the arena.

"Her internal monologue is blocked, so we'll have to rely on what they say aloud," Arraka whispers.

"I'm telling you, it isn't a loyalty test!" young Kate whispers urgently, glancing at the reinforced door. "I know this sounds impossible, but I came from the future. The Lessathi caretaker helping us escape becomes Leila's adoptive father. We can trust him!"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch11b-Collars, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11b-Collars)
